# Decide which repo files become resources, llms-full, and the three skills

## Step

Pick the exact file list the site serves: resources (`AGENTS.md`, `VISION.md`, `README.md`, `vendor/README.md`, the pins from `package.json` files, which `.brain/resources/*.svx`), the order and headings of `llms.txt`, whether `llms-full.txt` concatenates all of them, and the first three skills (recommendation: `add-a-capability`, `add-a-lifecycle-machine`, `keep-or-cut`) with their `SKILL.md` outlines. Boundary: only files in this public repo; nothing from dark-wizard, the operator Brain, or local skills.

## Direction (2026-09-21)

Joel: skills are site content, not just MCP prompts; see `aihero.dev/skills` for the shape. What that page does (observed 2026-09-21, `https://www.aihero.dev/skills.md` serves the same page as Markdown): one install command up top (`npx skills@latest add mattpocock/skills`), skills grouped by when you reach for them with a "start with" per group and a one-line promise per skill, each skill at its own URL, a "what is a skill" section, a changelog. Consequence for ratstack.sh: `/skills` is a page of its own in the content set, each skill is served at `/skills/<name>`, the agent-skills index at `/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json` is the machine form of the same list, and the install path is `npx skills add joelhooks/rat-stack` (the `skills` CLI reads `skills/*/SKILL.md` from the repo; verify in the prototype).
